my $CODE = <<'END_CODE';
foo bar foo baz foo
END_CODE

{
    desc => q{# searches backward for the word under cursor},
    description => <<'END_DESC',
## Macro: `xt/visual/macros/search_word_hash`

**#** searches backward for the whole word under the cursor. With cursor on the last "foo", it finds the previous occurrence.

**Keys:** `$hh#`

**initial.png**
- Cursor at line 1, col 0 (on 'f' of first "foo")
- Line: `foo bar foo baz foo`

**after_move_to_last.png**
- Cursor on last "foo" at col 16 (moved with `$hh`)

**after_hash.png**
- Cursor on second "foo" at col 8 (backward search from last "foo")
- All "foo" occurrences highlighted
- Search direction set to backward
END_DESC
    run => sub {
        my ($ctx) = @_;
        $ctx->buffer->set_text($CODE);
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('initial');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('$hh');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_move_to_last');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('#');
        $ctx->delay(300);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_hash');
    },
}
